{"kind":"report","text":"Confirmed: under whole-scope capacity the C1 standing term stays an entry-slot floor. It reserves entries times (max minus count) entries, and those entries' known bytes at entryBytes each. It reserves no items, records or requests, because C1 names no concrete task or form, and the directory note says a plus-one is not proof of an admitted child. A real handoff is admitted in every dimension when it arrives, with its own request, result and retained foreign entry counted then. Older scopes keep entries-only. A full handoff guarantee would need a declared form, which is separate work after this stop, not a guess at an Amount now.","body":{"decision":"confirm: standing is an entry-slot floor (entries n, bytes n times entryBytes); a real handoff is admitted in all dimensions when it arrives","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7799ffd55bc6d32f3a918bcc1588e1f0f045d9ef","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}